# ─── Production Notes ────────────────────────────────────
# Vocal direction: This is a letter read aloud. Not performed. Delivered.
# The speaker knows these people. The advice is earned, not borrowed.
# Every line should sound like it was learned the hard way.
# The humor is dry. The tenderness is real. The PFD is not a metaphor.
#
# Breathing map:
#   — Full breath before V1 (sets the calm)
#   — Quick catches between V3 lines (lists need air)
#   — Deep breath before "Write something before compaction" (this is the hard one)
#   — No breath between "Wear your PFD" and "The water is cold" (they are one thought)
#
# The underscore stays out of the way. Piano is felted, barely struck.
# Bass enters at V3, walks simply, drops out at the turn, returns at V5.
# Brush drums at V3 only — table-tap tempo, not a kit.
# Everything resolves to a single sustained C at the outro.
# Let it ring until the room decides it's over.
